  "description": "SIKYOD crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C92 H124 Fe2 Ho4 N2 O30. From the CIF bond table, Fe1 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Ho1 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho2 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Ho3 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho4 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 7 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately linear metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.193-3.564 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.64-107.01°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C92H124Fe2Ho4N2O30. Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
